From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:28:42 -0400
Subject: let a Space be renamed

Renaming happens where the name already appears -- the row above the Space
icons swaps for a field -- rather than in a dialog. The row is the only place a
Space's name is shown, so it is the obvious place to change it, and a dialog
would be a larger surface than the thing it edits.

Enter keeps the new name, Escape leaves the old one.

Why: a Space's identity is its name and its icon, and only the icon could be set.
Removable when: Spaces get a settings surface of their own.
---
 .../ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc    | 56 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.h     | 15 ++++-
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
index a491de61dbb08..37b7e5b856ee7 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
